-- Row il-42. THE FIGURES OF SECTION 9, BY PERIOD, AND WHERE EACH WAS READ.
--
-- Section 9 prints its amounts in a consolidation that is UNOFFICIAL. Each amount is carried here with the instrument it was read from.
-- Two statuses, nothing else, and the status is a typed value (`Where a figure was read`) that the tests check:
--   `read from the official page`   this encoder read the figure on the page image of the Knesset's PDF of Sefer HaChukim, the page named on the `ext:` line;
--   `the consolidation only`        CONSOLIDATION-ONLY: the Wikisource text (revision 3085765) or an editor's table inside it; no official page read.
--
-- INSTRUMENTS READ FROM THE PAGE IMAGE (this encoder, 2026-11-10, from images rendered with pdftoppm from the Knesset's PDFs deposited in `../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/`):
--   SH 5785 (Sefer HaChukim 3342, 26.12.2024) pp. 150-152, in the consolidation's header "Economic Efficiency Law (legislative amendments to achieve the budget targets of the 2025
--     budget year) (freeze of tax updates and surtax)", commencement 1 January 2025 (p. 152, s 3(a)):
--       p. 151, s 2(1)(a): the amounts of s 9(ג1ג)(1) and (3) are replaced by 1,465,800 / 4,397,380 / 6,055,070 / 20,183,565 and 1,978,745 / 2,347,040 / 6,055,070 / 20,183,565;
--       p. 151, s 2(1)(b): the amount of s 9(ג1ו) is replaced, in every place, by 6,055,070; s 2(1)(c): "except in tax years 2025 to 2027" is added to s 9(ג2), and the base
--         index of s 9(ג1ג) becomes the index published on 15 January 2027;
--       p. 151, s 2(2): the figure of s 49A(a1) becomes 5,008,000 and its base day 1 January 2027; p. 152, s 2(3): the figures of s 49E (2,252,000; 3,746,000) and the base day;
--         p. 152, s 2(4): the figures of s 49G(a) (2,428,100; 607,000) and the base index of 15 January 2027; p. 152, s 3(a): in force from 1 January 2025.
--   SH 5782 (Sefer HaChukim 2935, 28.11.2021) p. 460, Amendment 98 to the Law: s 9(ג1ו)(1): 8% up to 5,348,565 shekels and 10% above, for a dwelling bought from the Amendment's
--     commencement (28 November 2021) to 31 December 2024; (2): the Minister may by order, with the Finance Committee's approval, extend the period for a further two years.
--   SH 5773 (Sefer HaChukim 2405, 5.8.2013) pp. 154-156, the Law for Changing National Priorities (budget years 2013 and 2014), s 43(3)(d), which created s 9(ג1ג): for a dwelling bought from 1 August 2013
--     (then to 31 December 2014; Amendment 81, SH 5775 p. 190, made it "on 1 August 2013 or after", with effect from 1 August 2013): (1) 5% to 1,089,350; 6% to 3,268,040;
--     7% to 4,500,000; 8% to 15,000,000; 10% above; (3) nil to 1,470,560; 3.5% to 1,744,270; 5% to 4,500,000; 8% to 15,000,000; 10% above (the page image of pp. 155 and 156).
-- ALSO READ FROM THE PAGE IMAGE, by the lead of the session and not by this encoder, 2026-11-10: SH 5783 (Sefer HaChukim 3045, 31.5.2023) p. 161, s 10 ("18 months" for "24 months" in s 9(ג1ג)(2)(ב) and s 49ג(1),
--   for a period of two years from 12 Sivan 5783, 1 June 2023); SH 5783 (Sefer HaChukim 3063, 13.7.2023) p. 542, Amendment 103, ss 1 to 3 (a child orphaned of one or both parents, in s 9(ג1ג)(4)(ג) and s 49(ב);
--   it applies to rights bought or sold on or after the Amendment's commencement day, and the page names no commencement section: fork I1).
-- NOT READ: the Minister's order extending the (ג1ו) period (the consolidation's note cites Kovetz HaTakanot 5785 p. 626); the Director's annual notices under s 9(ג3);
--   the instruments that repealed s 9(ג1ד) and (ג1ה) (the consolidation prints both as repealed).
-- A ladder's percentages for 2025 are CONSOLIDATION-ONLY (the freeze law of SH 5785 replaces amounts only); its 2013 percentages were read from SH 5773 pp. 155-156.
--
-- THE LETTERS. The Law numbers the subsections of s 9 with Hebrew letters ("(ג1ג)" is gimel, 1, gimel). The names below keep the Law's own letters so a reader can find them.

§ `Figures of section 9`

§§ `The nouns of a ladder`

-- s 9(ג1ג)(1) and (3) print a ladder as a list of steps: "on the part of the value up to X – r%", "on the part of the value above X and up to Y – r%", and so on.
DECLARE `A step of a purchase-tax ladder` HAS
    `the step begins above` IS A NUMBER
    `the step ends at` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the rate on the part of the value in the step` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Which ladder of section 9` IS ONE OF
    `the general ladder of (ג1ג)(1)`
    `the single-dwelling ladder of (ג1ג)(3)`
    `the temporary ladder of (ג1ו)(1)`
    `the transitional general ladder of (ג1ב)(1)`
    `the transitional single-dwelling ladder of (ג1ב)(2)`

DECLARE `Where a figure was read` IS ONE OF
    `read from the official page`
    `the consolidation only`

-- The answer for a day: the steps, and where their amounts and their percentages were read.
DECLARE `A ladder in force on a day` HAS
    `its steps` IS A LIST OF `A step of a purchase-tax ladder`
    `where its amounts were read` IS A `Where a figure was read`
    `where its percentages were read` IS A `Where a figure was read`

§§ `The ladders as the Law prints them`

